undefined\",\"template\":[\"$\",\"$L3\",null,{}],\"templateStyles\":\"$undefined\",\"templateScripts\":\"$undefined\",\"notFound\":\"$undefined\",\"forbidden\":\"$undefined\",\"unauthorized\":\"$undefined\"}]]}],{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$1\",\"c\",{\"children\":[null,[\"$\",\"$L2\",null,{\"parallelRouterKey\":\"children\",\"error\":\"$undefined\",\"errorStyles\":\"$undefined\",\"errorScripts\":\"$undefined\",\"template\":[\"$\",\"$L3\",null,{}],\"templateStyles\":\"$undefined\",\"templateScripts\":\"$undefined\",\"notFound\":\"$undefined\",\"forbidden\":\"$undefined\",\"unauthorized\":\"$undefined\"}]]}],{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$1\",\"c\",{\"children\":[\"$L4\",[[\"$\",\"script\",\"script-0\",{\"src\":\"/_next/static/chunks/0xv9uz7g8af6d.js\",\"async\":true,\"nonce\":\"$undefined\"}]],[\"$\",\"$L5\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$6\",null,{\"name\":\"Next.MetadataOutlet\",\"children\":\"$@7\"}]}]]}],{},null,false,null]},null,false,\"$@8\"]},null,false,\"$@8\"]},null,false,\"$@8\"]},null,false,null],[\"$\",\"$1\",\"h\",{\"children\":[null,[\"$\",\"$L9\",null,{\"children\":\"$La\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"hidden\":true,\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Lb\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"$6\",null,{\"name\":\"Next.Metadata\",\"children\":\"$Lc\"}]}]}],[\"$\",\"meta\",null,{\"name\":\"next-size-adjust\",\"content\":\"\"}]]}],false]],\"m\":\"$undefined\",\"G\":[\"$d\",[[\"$\",\"link\",\"0\",{\"rel\":\"stylesheet\",\"href\":\"/_next/static/chunks/0-7zhabl4g7ue.css\",\"precedence\":\"next\",\"crossOrigin\":\"$undefined\",\"nonce\":\"$undefined\"}]]],\"S\":true,\"h\":null,\"s\":\"$undefined\",\"l\":\"$undefined\",\"p\":\"$undefined\",\"d\":\"$undefined\",\"b\":\"CCxR80sZRnjlIdOoXSFK7\"}\ne:[]\n8:\"$We\"\nf:I[22016,[\"/_next/static/chunks/01xlw8hd842-c.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0d3shmwh5_nmn.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0xv9uz7g8af6d.js\"],\"\"]\n10:I[16505,[\"/_next/static/chunks/01xlw8hd842-c.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0d3shmwh5_nmn.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0xv9uz7g8af6d.js\"],\"LessonClient\"]\n11:T8e1,# The Pipeline in Depth\n\nIn Module 1 you learned that the pipeline passes **objects** between cmdlets. Now let's master the cmdlets that make the pipeline truly powerful.\n\n## Filtering with Where-Object\n\n`Where-Object` filters objects based on a condition. The `$_` variable represents the **current object** in the pipeline:\n\n```powershell\nGet-Service | Where-Object { $_.Status -eq 'Running' }\nGet-Process | Where-Object { $_.CPU -gt 50 }\n```\n\n> **Key Concept:** `$_` (or `$PSItem`) is the automatic variable that refers to the current pipeline object. You'll use it constantly.\n\n## Selecting Properties with Select-Object\n\n`Select-Object` picks which properties to display or limits how many objects are returned:\n\n```powershell\nGet-Process | Select-Object Name, CPU, Id -First 5\nGet-Service | Select-Object -ExpandProperty Name\n```\n\n## Sorting and Grouping\n\n`Sort-Object` orders results, while `Group-Object` clusters them by a property value:\n\n```powershell\nGet-Process | Sort-Object CPU -Descending\nGet-Service | Group-Object Status\n```\n\n## Measuring with Measure-Object\n\n`Measure-Object` counts items or calculates sums, averages, minimums, and maximums:\n\n```powershell\nGet-Process | Measure-Object -Property CPU -Sum -Average\nGet-ChildItem | Measure-Object -Property Length -Sum\n```\n\n## ForEach-Object vs foreach\n\n`ForEach-Object` runs in the **pipeline** and processes items one at a time as they stream through. The `foreach` **statement** collects all items first, then iterates:\n\n```powershell\n# Pipeline version — streams objects\nGet-Service | ForEach-Object { $_.DisplayName.ToUpper() }\n\n# Statement version — collects all first, then loops\nforeach ($svc in Get-Service) {\n    $svc.DisplayName.ToUpper()\n}\n```\n\n> **Key Concept:** Use `ForEach-Object` (alias `%`) in pipelines for streaming. Use the `foreach` statement in scripts when you need the full collection or better performance on large datasets already in memory.\n\n## Chaining It All Together\n\nThe real power comes from combining these cmdlets into a single pipeline:\n\n```powershell\nGet-Process |\n    Where-Object { $_.CPU -gt 10 } |\n    Sort-Object CPU -Descending |\n    Select-Object Name, CPU -First 5\n```\n\nThis filters processes by CPU usage, sorts them highest-first, and returns the top 5.\n4:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"min-h-screen bg-zinc-950 text-zinc-100\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"header\",null,{\"className\":\"sticky top-0 z-10 border-b border-zinc-800/60 bg-zinc-950/80 backdrop-blur-xl\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mx-auto flex max-w-4xl items-center justify-between px-6 py-3.5\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$Lf\",null,{\"href\":\"/module/intermediate\",\"className\":\"inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-sm text-zinc-500 transition-colors hover:text-zinc-300\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"className\":\"h-4 w-4\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"path\",null,{\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"d\":\"M10.5 19.5L3 12m0 0l7.5-7.5M3 12h18\"}]}],\"Intermediate PowerShell\"]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"h-8 w-8\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-xs tabular-nums text-zinc-500\",\"children\":[1,\" / \",6]}],[\"$\",\"$Lf\",null,{\"href\":\"/module/intermediate/regex-and-strings\",\"className\":\"flex h-8 w-8 items-center justify-center rounded-lg border border-zinc-800 text-zinc-400 transition-colors hover:border-zinc-700 hover:text-zinc-200\",\"title\":\"Regular Expressions and Strings\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"className\":\"h-4 w-4\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"path\",null,{\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"d\":\"M8.25 4.5l7.5 7.5-7.5 7.5\"}]}]}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 pb-4\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"h1\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight\",\"children\":\"The Pipeline in Depth\"}]}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L10\",null,{\"lesson\":{\"meta\":{\"title\":\"The Pipeline in Depth\",\"description\":\"Where-Object, Select-Object, Sort-Object, ForEach-Object.\",\"slug\":\"pipeline-in-depth\",\"order\":1,\"prerequisites\":[]},\"content\":\"$11\",\"exercises\":[{\"id\":\"m2-l1-ex1\",\"type\":\"syntax-check\",\"prompt\":\"Write a pipeline that gets all services and filters to only those with a Status of 'Stopped'.\",\"hints\":[\"Start with Get-Service, then pipe to Where-Object.\",\"Use $_.Status inside the Where-Object script block.\",\"Try: Get-Service | Where-Object { $_.Status -eq 'Stopped' }\"],\"validation\":[{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"Get-Service\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Start with the Get-Service cmdlet.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"|\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use the pipe operator | to pass objects to the next cmdlet.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"Where-Object\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use Where-Object to filter the services.\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"\\\\$_\\\\.Status\\\\s+-eq\\\\s+['\\\"]Stopped['\\\"]\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Filter where $_.Status -eq 'Stopped'.\"}],\"solution\":\"Get-Service | Where-Object { $_.Status -eq 'Stopped' }\",\"explanation\":\"Get-Service retrieves all services. Where-Object filters the pipeline to only those objects where the Status property equals 'Stopped'.\"},{\"id\":\"m2-l1-ex2\",\"type\":\"syntax-check\",\"prompt\":\"Write a pipeline that gets all processes, sorts them by WorkingSet64 in descending order, and selects only the Name and WorkingSet64 properties of the first 3.\",\"hints\":[\"Chain three cmdlets: Get-Process, Sort-Object, and Select-Object.\",\"Sort-Object uses -Descending to reverse the order.\",\"Select-Object uses -First to limit the number of results.\"],\"validation\":[{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"Get-Process\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Start with Get-Process.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"Sort-Object\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Pipe to Sort-Object to sort the results.\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"WorkingSet64\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Sort by and select the WorkingSet64 property.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"-Descending\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use -Descending to sort from highest to lowest.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"Select-Object\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Pipe to Select-Object to pick properties.\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"-First\\\\s+3\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use -First 3 to return only the top 3 results.\"}],\"solution\":\"Get-Process | Sort-Object WorkingSet64 -Descending | Select-Object Name, WorkingSet64 -First 3\",\"explanation\":\"This pipeline sorts processes by memory usage (WorkingSet64) in descending order, then selects only the Name and WorkingSet64 properties of the top 3.\"},{\"id\":\"m2-l1-ex3\",\"type\":\"syntax-check\",\"prompt\":\"Write a pipeline that groups all services by their Status property using Group-Object.\",\"hints\":[\"Start with Get-Service and pipe to Group-Object.\",\"Group-Object takes a property name as its argument.\",\"Try: Get-Service | Group-Object Status\"],\"validation\":[{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"Get-Service\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Start with Get-Service.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"|\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use the pipe operator |.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"Group-Object\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use Group-Object to group items.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"Status\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Group by the Status property.\"}],\"solution\":\"Get-Service | Group-Object Status\",\"explanation\":\"Group-Object clusters the service objects by their Status property, showing you a count of how many services are Running, Stopped, etc.\"},{\"id\":\"m2-l1-ex4\",\"type\":\"syntax-check\",\"prompt\":\"Write a pipeline that uses Measure-Object to calculate the sum of the Length property for all files in the current directory (use Get-ChildItem).\",\"hints\":[\"Get-ChildItem lists items in the current directory.\",\"Pipe to Measure-Object with -Property Length and -Sum.\",\"Try: Get-ChildItem | Measure-Object -Property Length -Sum\"],\"validation\":[{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"Get-ChildItem\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use Get-ChildItem to list files.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"Measure-Object\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Pipe to Measure-Object to perform calculations.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"-Property\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use -Property to specify which property to measure.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"Length\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Measure the Length property for file sizes.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"-Sum\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Use -Sum to calculate the total.\"}],\"solution\":\"Get-ChildItem | Measure-Object -Property Length -Sum\",\"explanation\":\"This pipeline gets all items in the current directory and calculates the sum of their Length (file size) property using Measure-Object.\"},{\"id\":\"m2-l1-ex5\",\"type\":\"syntax-check\",\"prompt\":\"Write a pipeline that uses ForEach-Object to output the DisplayName of each service in uppercase.\",\"hints\":[\"Start with Get-Service and pipe to ForEach-Object.\",\"Access the DisplayName property with $_.DisplayName.\",\"Use the .ToUpper() method to convert to uppercase.\"],\"validation\":[{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"Get-Service\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Start with Get-Service.\"},{\"rule\":\"contains\",\"value\":\"ForEach-Object\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Pipe to ForEach-Object to process each item.\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"\\\\$_\\\\.DisplayName\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Access the DisplayName property with $_.DisplayName.\"},{\"rule\":\"regex\",\"pattern\":\"\\\\.ToUpper\\\\(\\\\)\",\"hintOnFail\":\"Call .ToUpper() to convert the string to uppercase.\"}],\"solution\":\"Get-Service | ForEach-Object { $_.DisplayName.ToUpper() }\",\"explanation\":\"ForEach-Object processes each service object in the pipeline. $_.DisplayName accesses the display name, and .ToUpper() converts it to uppercase.\"}],\"moduleSlug\":\"intermediate\"}}],\"$L12\"]}]\n12:[\"$\",\"footer\",null,{\"className\":\"border-t border-zinc-800/60\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mx-auto flex max-w-4xl items-center justify-between px-6 py-6\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{}],[\"$\",\"$Lf\",null,{\"href\":\"/module/intermediate/regex-and-strings\",\"className\":\"group flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-zinc-400 transition-colors hover:text-zinc-200\",\"children\":[\"Regular Expressions and Strings\",[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"className\":\"h-4 w-4 transition-transform group-hover:translate-x-0.5\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"strokeWidth\":2,\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"path\",null,{\"strokeLinecap\":\"round\",\"strokeLinejoin\":\"round\",\"d\":\"M13.5 4.5L21 12m0 0l-7.5 7.5M21 12H3\"}]}]]}]]}]}]\na:[[\"$\",\"meta\",\"0\",{\"charSet\":\"utf-8\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"1\",{\"name\":\"viewport\",\"content\":\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\"}]]\n13:I[27201,[\"/_next/static/chunks/01xlw8hd842-c.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/0d3shmwh5_nmn.js\"],\"IconMark\"]\n7:null\nc:[[\"$\",\"title\",\"0\",{\"children\":\"PowerShell Training\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"1\",{\"name\":\"description\",\"content\":\"Interactive PowerShell training — from basics to SharePoint administration.\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"2\",{\"rel\":\"icon\",\"href\":\"/favicon.ico?favicon.0x3dzn~oxb6tn.ico\",\"sizes\":\"256x256\",\"type\":\"image/x-icon\"}],[\"$\",\"$L13\",\"3\",{}]]\n","segmentData":{"/_tree":":HL[\"/_next/static/chunks/0-7zhabl4g7ue.css\",\"style\"]\n:HL[\"/_next/static/media/797e433ab948586e-s.p.0.q-h669a_dqa.woff2\",\"font\",{\"crossOrigin\":\"\",\"type\":\"font/woff2\"}]\n:HL[\"/_next/static/media/caa3a2e1cccd8315-s.p.16t1db8_9y2o~.woff2\",\"font\",{\"crossOrigin\":\"\",\"type\":\"font/woff2\"}]\n0:{\"tree\":{\"name\":\"\",\"param\":null,\"prefetchHints\":16,\"slots\":{\"chi